          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Operations with Integers"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.087,
            0.846,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can you summarise the rules for integer division looking at the above pattern?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.132,
            0.846,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In general, for any two positive integers a and b, where "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b \\neq 0 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , we can say that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.387,
            0.171,
            0.598,
            0.239
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}&\\mathbf{a} \\div -\\mathbf{b} = -(\\mathbf{a} \\div \\mathbf{b}), \\\\&-\\mathbf{a} \\div \\mathbf{b} = -(\\mathbf{a} \\div \\mathbf{b}),  and  \\\\&-\\mathbf{a} \\div -\\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{a} \\div \\mathbf{b}.\\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.255,
            0.315,
            0.28
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.289,
            0.686,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the values of: (a) 14 × (– 15) (b) – 16 × (– 5) (c) 36 ÷ (– 18) (d) (– 46) ÷ (– 23)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.369,
            0.846,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. A freezing process requires that the room temperature be lowered from "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 2 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " at the rate of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " every hour. What will be the room temperature 10 hours after the process begins?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.432,
            0.847,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. A cement company earns a profit of ₹8 per bag of white cement sold and a loss of ₹5 per bag of grey cement sold. [Represent the profit/ loss as integers.]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.495,
            0.847,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) The company sells 3,000 bags of white cement and 5,000 bags of grey cement in a month. What is its profit or loss?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.539,
            0.847,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) If the number of bags of grey cement sold is 6,400 bags, what is the number of bags of white cement the company must sell to have neither profit nor loss."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.602,
            0.769,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Replace the blank with an integer to make a true statement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.627,
            0.391,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) (– 3) × _ = 27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.627,
            0.714,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) 5 × _ = (– 35)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.652,
            0.417,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) × (– 8) = (– 56)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.652,
            0.738,
            0.671
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(d) × (– 12) = 132"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.676,
            0.384,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(e) ÷ (– 8) = 7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.514,
            0.677,
            0.712,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(f) ÷ 12 = – 11"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.725,
            0.482,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Expressions Using Integers"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.756,
            0.846,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ What is the value of the expression 5 × – 3 × 4? Does it matter whether we multiply 5 × – 3 and then multiply the product with 4, or if we multiply – 3 × 4 first and then multiply the product with 5?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.329,
            0.827,
            0.441,
            0.884
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_19.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{array} { l } { { \\begin{array} { l } { ( 5 \\times - 3 ) \\times 4 } \\\\ { \\quad = - 1 5 \\times 4 } \\\\ { \\quad = - 6 0 . } \\end{array} } } \\end{array}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.561,
            0.826,
            0.672,
            0.884
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_20.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{array} { l } { { 5 \\times ( - 3 \\times 4 ) } } \\\\ { { \\quad = 5 \\times - 1 2 } } \\\\ { { \\quad = - 6 0 . } } \\end{array}"
        },
